# API conventions

Put product routes under `/api/v1`. Interpret an image with `POST /api/v1/interpretations`.

- Require `Authorization: Bearer` and the scope `interpretations:write`.
- Accept `multipart/form-data` with one `image` file: JPEG, PNG, or WebP, up to 10 MB.
- Return `200` with this stable JSON: `id`, `summary`, `objects[]` (`label`, `confidence`, `description`), `extractedText[]` (`text`, `confidence`), overall `confidence` from 0 to 1, `model.provider`, and `model.name`.
- For failures, use only `400`, `401`, `403`, `413`, `415`, `422`, or `503`.
- Send errors as RFC 7807 problem details. Do not add schema fields that `docs/specs/003-api-contracts.md` and `docs/specs/004-data-model.md` do not define.

Bad: a custom error body and a field outside the contract.

```json
{ "message": "file too large", "vendor": "some-model" }
```

Good: RFC 7807 problem details and an allowed status.

```json
{
  "type": "about:blank",
  "title": "Payload Too Large",
  "status": 413,
  "detail": "The image is larger than 10 MB."
}
```
